.SH NAME
le-stop - Stop a listener the smart way (TERM / brew / docker)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle stop  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop every listener on a port (or the process with a PID), each via its
recommended strategy. The PID is re-checked first, so a recycled PID is
never the one that gets signalled.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBle(1)\fP


